# 6. BACKEND LOGIC AND BUSINESS RULES

Implement the actual backend operations using Firebase Cloud Functions and secure Firestore access.

At minimum, implement:

1. Secure order creation.
2. Server-side price calculation.
3. Server-side discount validation.
4. Stock validation.
5. Inventory reservation or deduction using transactions.
6. Payment submission.
7. Payment verification by an administrator.
8. Order status updates.
9. Delivery fee calculation.
10. Stock restoration for eligible cancelled orders.
11. Admin-only product management.
12. Admin-only category management.
13. Admin-only discount management.
14. Admin-only store settings management.
15. Customer order retrieval with ownership checks.
16. Admin dashboard statistics.
17. Notification creation.

All sensitive business operations must be validated on the server.

The server must calculate totals from trusted product, discount, and delivery data. Never trust totals, product prices, roles, or payment statuses supplied by the browser.

Use atomic transactions where multiple database records must remain consistent.

Use idempotency protections where appropriate so repeated requests cannot accidentally create duplicate orders or payments.

